/**
 * @page topic_client_audio Client Audio
 * @ingroup module_client
 * @brief Capture, encode, transmit, and play audio through the shared pipeline.
 *
 * Client audio uses the common audio and ACIP layers. Capture produces PCM or
 * encoded audio batches; playback consumes received batches through audio
 * ring/jitter buffers and the platform output backend.
 *
 * @section client_audio_capture Capture and send
 *
 * The capture path negotiates sample format, rate, and channels with the active
 * backend. It sends with `acip_send_audio_batch()`, the Opus helpers, or another
 * type-specific ACIP API through `network_connection_transport()`. It does not
 * call the removed `send_packet_to_server()` API.
 *
 * @section client_audio_playback Playback
 *
 * Incoming audio is validated by ACIP handlers, converted to the local channel
 * layout when necessary, and written to a bounded ring buffer. The output
 * callback reads from that buffer and fills underruns with silence. Realtime
 * callbacks must not allocate, log, block, or perform network work.
 *
 * @section client_audio_visualization Visualizations
 * The shared visualization encoder applies the configured palette, color mode,
 * and foreground, background, or half-block rendering before frames reach the browser.
 *
 * Waveform and FFT visualizations consume the selected audio source and are
 * controlled by TUI shortcuts. They are presentation consumers, not a second
 * capture or transport path.
 *
 * @see topic_audio
 * @see topic_mixer
 * @see topic_client_connection
 */
